  "caption": "Quinn's knees have started creaking, the couch has become a three-act drama, and the jar lid keeps winning.\n\nLiving with osteoarthritis often means good days and flare days. Flares come and go, and they don't mean the joint is getting worse. The idea is to reduce the load, not the movement.\n\nDaily tweaks that can help: a warm shower for morning stiffness, a higher seat that is easier to stand from, jar grips and two-handed carrying, pacing jobs into chunks, keeping up strength training, and a walking stick in the opposite hand if it helps you stay active.\n\nIf pain is changing how you live or work, get it checked. Questions about pain relief or surgery are best discussed with your GP.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
